From d4e66dad202aabcef463bf83e0638f6a79a2aa3e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 8 Jul 2026 04:39:43 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(offline): update status/features/actions after offline
 run writes
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Offline, pausing a run / creating an issue / capturing a missing photo persisted
locally (offlineStore.saveRun) but the Assets page never re-rendered — status,
feature widgets and the action button kept showing the pre-change state until the
app went back online. Online it worked.

Root cause: the Assets page refreshes its runsMap on the
"workflow-runs-cache-updated" event, but that event was only dispatched by
refreshRunsInBackground / refreshRunByIdInBackground, which both early-return on
shouldSkipBlockingFetch() (offline) and only fire after a successful network GET.
So offline writes produced no refresh signal.

Added signalLocalRunUpdate(run): dispatched on every offline write path (after
offlineStore.saveRun in saveProgress, patchIssues, patchStepResults/A1,
completeRun, time-entry, and run-create) with { assetId, runs:[run], mergeById }.
The Assets page listener now, when mergeById is set, replaces that one run by id and
keeps the rest of the asset's run history intact (instead of clobbering the
list) — so status/features/actions update immediately offline without a network
round-trip, and run history is preserved.

Client-only, no backend, no api.ts change. Two files. tsc -b + build clean.
Note: needs device verification (offline pause/issue/photo → display updates).
